The first self-test exposed a performance bug in the test harness, not the generator: the 200,000-sample density check rebuilt the same cycle-position dictionary on every guess. I’ve stopped that run and am caching only deterministic construction data and the precomputed position map; the verifier itself remains a generic BFS over the stated graph.
