codex
Step 0 supports a Track B family, not Track A. Section 4 defines \(r\)-Dominating Set exactly; Lemma 4.1 supplies the bounded-treewidth DP encoder, and Theorem 4.2 gives the constructive linear kernel for fixed \(r\) on apex-minor-free graphs. But the generated regime will be trees, where an exact deepest-undominated-vertex algorithm produces a certificate in polynomial time—so hiding that algorithm would make Track A false.

The construction I’m proceeding with samples the dominating set first, builds a tree from radius-\(r\) neighborhoods around it, and then applies a reversible vertex relabelling. The planned shipping gap is roughly tens of thousands of tree-scan operations versus at most 241 bit/integer operations after noticing the coordinate change; I’ll replace the estimate with measured numbers before declaring the module complete.
